      "confidence": 0.95,
      "evidence": [
        "ae_ip_by_year.csv: A/E falls from 1.21 (2015-2017) to 0.814 (2018), 0.239 (2019), and 0.357 (2020), then jumps to 1.232 (2021) and stabilizes at ~1.25 (2022-2024)",
        "Computed evidence pack: shaped-pulse excursion (2019-2020, -0.880, score 11.1) with x15.16 overdispersion driven entirely by the level change, not independent volatility",
        "Cross-line check: only IP deviates >0.08 from baseline; Death, CI, and TPD show no strong signal and remain within Poisson-valid noise"
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Investigate 2018/2019 data feed, policy admin, or benefit design changes that caused the sharp A/E drop; verify whether the 2021 rebound reflects actual claim activity, backlog run-off, or assumption/model updates; review IP pricing and reserving for the new sustained ~1.25 A/E post-2020"
    }
  ]
}

